      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Humidity can definitely affect printing results, especially with sublimation ink. Using a dehumidifier to maintain optimal humidity levels for your printing environment could help. Also, consider experimenting with slightly lower temperatures or longer drying times to see if they maintain better ink adherence consistently. It might also be worth exploring different ink brand or formulation that is specifically claimed to work better in various humidity conditions. If common remedies fail, it could be an issue with your printer, and a service technician might need to be called in.",
