    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk man the humidity is steady. i even checked the ink storage too. it's just so random. like we'll have a perfect run and then suddenly it's like the color just vanishes from the middle of a sheet. it's almost like someone is messing with it or something is interfering with the transfer mid-press. any idea what else could cause that kind of \"disappearing\" effect?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"disappearing\" effect you're describing could potentially be due to several issues. Check for any loose belts, rollers, or a failed sublimation paper that could cause inconsistency. Make sure the prints are fed straight into the press as any sideways feeding can cause the ink to seem like it's missing. Also consider if the sublimation paper is being preheated properly and the platen is evenly heating; this can sometimes cause varying degrees of transfer. If all of these are in check, there may be a problem with the heat press itself, such as a failing component. Tracking down and replacing faulty parts may be required. If you are unsure about any steps or need professional support, don’t hesitate to contact the manufacturer or a professional technician.",
